{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/608651-paris-starter-game","id":608651,"title":"Paris starter game","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-07-30T17:36:37-07:00","id":608651,"title":"Paris starter game","content":"So I'm looking for ideas for a Paris based Mummy Chronicle. Here's some vague ideas I've already had and some stuff I definitely wanna include.<br /> <br /> 1. There are rumors that Paris was named after Isis (Paris= Per-Aset, or &quot;House of Isis&quot; in English). Seems unlikely. More reasonable arguments say there was once a Roman temple to Isis in Paris back in the day. Some claim that temple was under the St. Germain Church, others that it is buried beneath Notre Dame (ironic!). Whether true or not, it seems a good reason to have a few mummies and/or Scorpion cultists migrate to the city.<br /> <br /> 2. The Templars of course once had a Temple in Paris. Popular legend says they were forced to flee before they could collect their vast stores of Middle Eastern wealth. Seems like a good place to start in terms of Relics.<br /> <br /> 3. The alchemist Cagliostri introduced &quot;Egyptian Masonry&quot; to certain areas including Paris. He was also involved in the Affair of the Necklace, a scandal that placed a wedge between Marie Antoinette and the common people. Said wedge contributed to a certain Revolution not too long after the incident.<br /> <br /> 4. It seems clear to me that something important happened with regard to the Arisen during the French Revolution. Historically Napoleon rose to power and invaded Egypt (among other conquests). That sparked the modern era of Egyptomania, and led to the discovery of Rosetta stone. Also, an Egyptian monolith was placed at the center of the Place de la Concorde, an area that among other architectural features supposedly aligns with the rising of the Sothic Star. Exactly what took place here is something I could use some advice on.<br /> <br /> 5. The Louvre began collecting Egyptian artifacts not long after the end of the Revolution. Originally a palace for the king, the Museum is confirmed to have many secret doors as well as a wealth of exhibits from around the world. If your looking for a meeting place for the Nome and/or an easy way to build a potent Lifeweb in the city.....there you have it.<br /> <br /> 6. The famous orient express had its start (or terminus, depending on perspective) in Paris. This practically demands some mummies wake up en route somewhere on the express at some point. Also, strictly because I like the idea and it seems appropo to the Guild, a Maa-Kep has made it a personal mission to maintain the railroad, which is why it is still running in my WOD as opposed to the shitty real world where it is not. :C<br /> <br /> 7. Paris in general seems like the kinda place the Mesen-Nebu are going to love to congregate at. Therefore, majority presence in the city.I'd say the same about the Tef-Abhi.<br /> <br /> 8. The catacombs seem like a good hangout for the Su-Menent. Among other things.<br /> <br /> 9. Canonically there is an original copy of Dreams of Avarice hidden in a vault beneath the city. Also a mummy named Taweret that has read it several times.<br /> <br /> <br /> More thoughts about NPCs, theats...anything at all...fire at will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2244-nothri","name":"nothri","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"485"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}